author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "--full, --json, custom or partial omission receipts, unreadable completeness and non-default sorting are unchanged, and the projections stay pure SDK exports that leave their input unchanged; A spec measures the TOON bytes of --fields id,title against the default brief page on the same corpus and asserts the --fields envelope is not larger; Negative control: reverting either projection to brief-only recognition fails the spec; pm search with or without --fields prints only explicitly set filters (no default-valued filter keys) in TOON and JSON, and its TOON page carries no projection echo, no now, no truncated alias, no mode_source the caller already knows and details --full; pm list with --fields or --compact prints the lean TOON envelope of the default brief page: no truncated when it equals has_more, no projection echo while rows show the fields, no filters.limit equal to applied_limit and no filters.fields equal to the projection, no now, completeness reduced to its status line, sorting as one effective_keys line, and details --full instead of the default full_item_fields omission receipt"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
repro_steps: "In any tracker with more than three open items, compare the byte size of pm list --status open --limit 3 with the same command plus --fields id,title or --compact, and pm search <query> --limit 3 with and without --fields id,title"
resolution: "projectPmBriefListEnvelope and projectPmBriefSearchEnvelope (src/sdk/output/list-envelope.ts) now recognize any standard row projection (mode brief, compact or fields with a non-empty field list) instead of only the exact brief field list, and they require every row to carry exactly the projected keys, so a producer whose echo disagrees with its rows passes through unchanged. The projection echo is dropped because the row header lists the fields; an empty --fields page keeps it. A filters.fields echo equal to the projection is dropped, and on --fields search pages so are now and a mode_source other than settings. SDK runSearch with a fields projection echoes filters through the same set-only summary as the compact default (buildProjectedSearchFilters), so search --fields JSON no longer carries 13 default-valued keys; --full keeps the verbose echo. Kept by contract: completeness keeps its status line (pm-6pycus), and items_encoding keeps json_columns and absent because decoders detect an encoding block by them. On this tracker, list --fields id,title went from 1,296 B to 887 B, --compact from 1,274 B to 957 B, and search --fields id,title from 1,036 B to 444 B."
expected_result: "pm list --fields/--compact and pm search --fields TOON pages carry no truncated alias, projection echo, now, limit/fields filter echo or four-line omission receipt, and are no larger in envelope than the default brief page; search --fields JSON echoes only set filters"
actual_result: "Verified on this repository's tracker (byte table in the resolution) and by tests/integration/read-output/projection-envelopes.integration.spec.ts, which runs the built CLI and asserts envelope bytes are no larger than the brief page, plus 77 compact-agent-output specs. Negative control: reverting list-envelope.ts to brief-only recognition fails 4 specs. Full quality:static chain minus mutation passed; focused coverage of the changed modules is 100% on every changed line."
affected_version: 2026.11.5
component: list
