comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T07:59:32.520Z","harness:claude-code","Review follow-up (CodeRabbit round 3 on PR #1675): the fields-versus-full filter selection was duplicated between emptySearchResult and buildProjectedSearchFilters. It now lives in buildProjectedSearchFilters, which takes a SearchFilterEchoInput (a Pick of SearchResponseContext), so the hit, empty and count-only paths share one selection. No behaviour change; search specs and the projection-envelope integration spec pass (362 tests)."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T04:48:52.041Z","harness:claude-code","Scope decisions made during implementation (2026-11-06). (1) items_encoding keeps json_columns and absent even when both are empty. The table-rows spec's own TOON decoder recognizes an encoding block by checking that both are arrays, and external hosts that decode TOON tables can use the same signature, so omitting them would break table detection for about 37 B per table. pm-gh1642 kept the block for the same reason. (2) completeness unchecked stays visible as one status line, because pm-6pycus requires that unchecked or partial source evidence never disappears; only the two zero unreadable counts are dropped. (3) JSON list envelopes are unchanged: default and --fields JSON already differ only by the filters.fields echo. JSON search --fields now echoes only the filters the caller set, through the same compact summary the default search uses, and keeps projection, now and mode_source in the typed result. (4) A projection whose field list disagrees with the row keys is treated as inconsistent and passes through unchanged, so the compaction never hides a producer mismatch."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T05:08:17.377Z","harness:claude-code","A presentation compaction keyed to one exact projection shape silently stops applying to every sibling projection. projectPmBriefListEnvelope accepted only mode brief with the exact BRIEF_LIST_FIELDS, so --fields, --compact and a brief page led by another sort field all fell through to the verbose envelope, and the narrower projection cost more than the default. Recognize the projection class (mode plus field list), then bind the echo to the rows: every row must carry exactly the projected keys, otherwise the projection is inconsistent and passes through. Measure each sibling projection against the default on the same corpus in a spec, so the next new projection mode cannot regress unnoticed."
